expect:
I would expect the work to be about how choosing-processes (rewards, markets, votes, AI training) can wear out what they depend on without noticing, how they lock onto what is already winning, and how to set up human-and-AI decision-making so that this wearing-out is felt early and the process is not captured by those who benefit from running it. I would expect general theory first and AI as one case of it.

In my own writing here I would watch for:
- not describing a selection as a separate agent standing outside the world and acting on it; it is one process among the others;
- not using seeing or knowing words for it (the paragraph says "makes a difference to", never "sees");
- saying when something changes and whether that is early enough, not only that it changes;
- not claiming more than is there.

I would also worry that copying this style would make my writing hard to follow.
